caption: Context
title: Context
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

! Summary
A context describes where or how an action happens. Unlike the other types, contexts are ordinary tags whose tiddlers are tagged ''GSD/Contexts'' — the tag list ''is'' the dashboard tiddler, so an action can carry several contexts at once, using core tagging mechanics.

! Detail

!! Using contexts
* Tag any action with a listed context tag (via the modal's context picker, the contextualise button on the action's row, or the tag box).
* The contextualise button also creates contexts: a typed name matching no tiddler is created tagged `GSD/Contexts` and applied to the action in one step.
* The modal offers the caller's contexts as defaults; the capture sidebar's context select seeds new captures.
* Contexts are excluded for contacts and references.

!! Field Variables

| !Field | !Values | !Note |
|gsd_context |''context tag'' |Modal seeding: selected context tag |

!! UI Controls
The context view template shows the context's actions; the Contexts dashboard lists every listed context.

! Best Practice
List a context by tagging its tiddler with `GSD/Contexts` (or typing its name on the [[GSD/Contexts]] dashboard) — an unlisted tag still works as a plain TiddlyWiki tag but stays invisible to the pickers and dashboards.